// Boom and bust -- the owner's two lab playtests of 2026-10-07, as a box.
//
// Both playtests ran the same way: a colony landed beside more food than it
// could eat, grew until it had eaten it (playtest 1: 104 -> 1,432 ants in
// 80k frames, the larder from 8.0M J to 12k), then crashed -- every adult
// dead within 20k frames, the brood starving. The owner: *"I feel like we
// need to slow down birth ... we cannot build up food because our
// population grows quickly as we get more food"*.
//
// So: the nest goal's box and colony (no plants, mister off, 52 ants at
// column 256 at frame 6,000), and a large store of provisions east of the
// nest that nothing ever refills: 2,000 cells at provisions' 960 J is
// 1.92M J, the order of the playtests' larders on the gut-0 price. **Two
// heaps of 1,000, at columns 330 and 420, not one of 2,000 at 286**: a
// `Heap` is a pyramid (row r is 2r+1 wide), so 2,000 cells is 89 columns
// across and centred 30 east of the door it would bury the nest. These
// two span about 299-361 and 389-451, the nearer edge 43 columns out.
// Run it in `deeptrace` with `food=0`, or the harness's `top_up` refills
// the heap and this becomes the nest goal again.
//
// **What a fix looks like here is not survival** -- finite food that never
// comes back ends every colony. It is the shape of the end: births slowing
// as the store shrinks and a colony that falls gradually, against today's
// boom to the peak and a crash from it with the larvae starving.
(
    name: "boom_bust",
    title: "BOOM AND BUST",
    question: "A big store of food that never comes back: does the colony slow its births as the store runs down, or breed to the peak and crash?",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 80,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 1,
        founders: 0,
        species: "grass",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 52,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [
        (subject: "the bed", field: "rain", value: 0),
    ],
    placements: [],
    timeline: [
        (at: 6000, every: 0, until: 0, what: Colony(species: "ant", x: 256, count: 52)),
        (at: 6000, every: 0, until: 0, what: Heap(material: "provisions", x: 330, cells: 1000)),
        (at: 6000, every: 0, until: 0, what: Heap(material: "provisions", x: 420, cells: 1000)),
    ],
    horizon: 600000,
)
